// =============================================================================
// 07: "TEXAS SHUFFLE" — SLOW BURNING 12-BAR BLUES (Key of D / Bm — 40 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// Simpler, slower, spacious 12-bar blues backing track in the Key of D / Bm.
// Relaxed 40 CPM crawl tempo with ample room for crying bends and deep vibrato.
//
// 🎸 HOW TO JAM OVER KEY OF D / Bm:
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • D Minor Pentatonic + The Blue Note (Box 1, 10th Fret):
//    e |--------------------------------10--13--|  (D, F)
//    B |------------------------10--13----------|  (A, C)
//    G |----------------10--12-[13]-------------|  (F, G, [Ab = The Blue Note!])
//    D |--------10--12--------------------------|  (C, D)
//    A |----10--12-[13]-------------------------|  (G, A, [Ab])
//    E |--10--13--------------------------------|  (D, F)
//
// • B.B. King Sweet Box (D Major Pentatonic / B Minor Pentatonic, 10th-12th Fret):
//    e |--------10--12--|  (D, E)
//    B |--10-12---------|  (A, B) -> Bend 12th fret on B (B up to C#) for sweet blues cry!
//
// • Iconic Slow Blues Opening Lick in D:
//   Slow whole-step bend on 12th fret of G string (G bent up to A), hold with
//   heavy vibrato, release slowly to 10th fret G (F note), resolve to 12th fret D (D root)!
//
// 🎼 12-BAR HARMONIC ROADMAP (KEY OF D):
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Bar 1–4 : [D9] [G9] [D9] [D9]   -> Tonic with Quick-Change to IV in Bar 2
// Bar 5–6 : [G9] [G9]             -> IV Chord (Dig into crying bends!)
// Bar 7–8 : [D9] [D9]             -> Back to Tonic
// Bar 9   : [A9]                  -> V Chord (Peak emotional tension!)
// Bar 10  : [G9]                  -> Resolving IV Chord
// Bar 11  : [D9]                  -> Tonic
// Bar 12  : [A9]                  -> The Turnaround (Dripping tension back to Bar 1)
//
// 🎛️ CONTROLS (<leader> = Space in Neovim):
//   <leader>ml : :StrudelLaunch (Connect to Strudel engine)
//   <leader>mp : :StrudelToggle (Play / Pause backing track)
//   <leader>mu : :StrudelUpdate (APPLY CHANGES LIVE — Press after uncommenting!)
//   gcc        : Toggle comment on a line (1 tap to introduce/mute a layer)
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// 🌧️ TRACK 1: "TEXAS SHUFFLE" (Slow 12-Bar Blues Crawl — Key of D — 40 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// LIVE-BUILDING FLOW:
//   Starts with ONLY Layer 1 active (warm D9 blues chords with deep hall reverb).
//   Play your guitar intro over the chords, then introduce layers one-by-one:
//   Line 53: Walking Bass | Line 56: Shuffle Hat | Line 59: Snare | Line 62: Kick

stack(
  // [Step 1 - ACTIVE AT START] Warm Slow Blues Chords (D9 - G9 - A9)
  note("<[d3,fs3,c4,e4] [g2,b2,f3,a3] [d3,fs3,c4,e4]!2 [g2,b2,f3,a3]!2 [d3,fs3,c4,e4]!2 [a2,cs3,g3,b3] [g2,b2,f3,a3] [d3,fs3,c4,e4] [a2,cs3,g3,b3]>")
    .s("triangle")
    .lpf(1000)
    .room(0.85)
    .decay(1.4)
    .gain(0.42),

  // [Step 2 - BASS] Classic Swung Blues Walking / Boogie Bass (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[d2 fs2 a2 b2] [g1 b1 d2 e2] [d2 fs2 a2 b2]!2 [g1 b1 d2 e2]!2 [d2 fs2 a2 b2]!2 [a1 cs2 e2 fs2] [g1 b1 d2 e2] [d2 fs2 a2 b2] [a1 cs2 e2 fs2]>").s("triangle").lpf(340).decay(0.6).gain(0.68),

  // [Step 3 - SHUFFLE] Swung Triplet Blues Hi-Hat: 1 - a, 2 - a, 3 - a, 4 - a (Press gcc here)
  // s("[hh ~ hh]!4").gain(0.28),

  // [Step 4 - SNARE] Deep backbeat snare on 2 & 4 with hall reverb (Press gcc here)
  // s("~ sd ~ sd").room(0.75).gain(0.68),

  // [Step 5 - KICK] Heartbeat pulse on beat 1 & 3 (Press gcc here to anchor!)
  // s("bd ~ bd ~").lpf(280).gain(0.55),

  // [Step 6 - ORGAN] Hammond B3 Leslie swell (Press gcc here for extra blues soul!)
  // note("<[d3,a3,c4,fs4] [g2,g3,b3,f4] [d3,a3,c4,fs4]!2 [g2,g3,b3,f4]!2 [d3,a3,c4,fs4]!2 [a2,g3,cs4,e4] [g2,g3,b3,f4] [d3,a3,c4,fs4] [a2,g3,cs4,e4]>").s("sine").lpf(sine.range(700, 1500).slow(8)).room(0.9).gain(0.28),
).cpm(40)


